            <div xml:id="d10-a2">

                <pb facs="0191" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv08/pg181"/>

                <head>Appendix B to HD–51</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="4" xml:id="d10-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Draft Reply to the German Note of
                        September 5, Prepared by M. Nagaoha</hi>]</p>
                <p>The German Government, recognizing that the provision in article 61 of the
                    constitutional law of August 11, 1919, is in contradiction to the terms of
                    article 80 of the Treaty of Peace of June 28, 1919, and that the maintenance of
                    the said provision of article 61 before an appropriate assent has been given by
                    the Council of the League of Nations, might give rise to misunderstandings, in
                    spite of the provisions of article 178 of the said constitutional law, declares,
                    after approval by the Reichstag, that article 61, as well as all stipulations
                    contrary to the Treaty of Peace, are null and void.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
